{
  "name": "CI Agent · B - Weekly Analyst Brief",
  "nodes": [
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## Workflow B — Weekly Analyst Agent + Human Approval\nEvery Monday the AI Agent (Gemini) reads the log, compares with last month and searches the web, then writes a partner-style brief: headline moves, SWOT delta, threats/opportunities and 3 actions. Telegram notifies you, and the brief arrives by email with **Approve / Decline** buttons. Approved briefs are marked **final**, emailed via Gmail and logged in the `Briefs` data table.",
        "width": 640,
        "height": 240,
        "color": 4
      },
      "id": "e2f1dcdf-7ee3-4463-80a9-a405517d149e",
      "name": "Note a8a72d",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -200,
        -420
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "rule": {
          "interval": [
            {
              "field": "weeks",
              "triggerAtDay": [
                1
              ],
              "triggerAtHour": 9
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      "id": "199b83cb-eae3-4cd7-a939-6f12a2bd1fc9",
      "name": "Every Monday 9 AM",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.scheduleTrigger",
      "typeVersion": 1.2,
      "position": [
        0,
        0
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "assignments": {
          "assignments": [
            {
              "id": "34d3bb14-6244-4fc1-b000-c0d0dd336213",
              "name": "telegram_chat_id",
              "value": "PASTE_YOUR_TELEGRAM_CHAT_ID",
              "type": "string"
            },
            {
              "id": "0266ccd4-c2a5-49b6-a121-cdfc6e9b6d15",
              "name": "brief_email",
              "value": "PASTE_RECIPIENT_EMAIL",
              "type": "string"
            }
          ]
        },
        "options": {}
      },
      "id": "db3dbe2e-745b-425b-9401-5d943e70f81b",
      "name": "Config",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.set",
      "typeVersion": 3.4,
      "position": [
        220,
        0
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "promptType": "define",
        "text": "=Today is {{ $now.toFormat('cccc, dd LLL yyyy') }}. Write this week's brief for the week starting {{ $now.minus({days: 7}).toFormat('dd LLL yyyy') }}.",
        "options": {
          "systemMessage": "You are a partner at a strategy consultancy writing the weekly competitive-intelligence brief for the Head of Product and the Head of Marketing of a company competing in the product-management / work-management software market (Notion, Atlassian Jira & Confluence, Asana, monday.com, Linear and similar tools).\n\nMethod:\n1. Call read_intel_log and focus on items whose `date` falls in the last 7 days (also use older items for context).\n2. Call compare_with_last_month with \"all\" to see month-over-month changes in activity.\n3. Use web_search only to verify or add context to the most important moves (max 3 searches).\n4. Ignore items with is_relevant = false or impact_score below 4 unless they form a pattern.\n\nWrite the brief in Markdown with exactly these sections:\n# Weekly Competitive Intelligence Brief — <week>\n## 1. Headline moves\n3-5 bullets: what changed, who, and why it matters (cite the impact score).\n## 2. SWOT delta per competitor\nFor each competitor with activity: one line each for new Strengths, Weaknesses, Opportunities, Threats revealed this week (write \"no change\" where nothing moved).\n## 3. Threats and opportunities for us\n## 4. Three recommended actions\nNumbered 1-3. Each: the action, owner (Product / Marketing / Leadership), priority (High/Medium), and why now.\n## 5. Sources\nBullet list of the links you relied on.\n\nRules: be concise and specific, no generic advice, never invent facts or links — if the week was quiet, say so. Mark recommendations as DRAFT; a human approves them before they become final.",
          "maxIterations": 12
        }
      },
      "id": "e8f41d9b-4478-431d-bf10-45a1bfbef6a3",
      "name": "Analyst Agent",
      "type": "@n8n/n8n-nodes-langchain.agent",
      "typeVersion": 2.2,
      "position": [
        460,
        0
      ],
      "retryOnFail": true,
      "maxTries": 3,
      "waitBetweenTries": 5000
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "modelName": "models/gemini-flash-lite-latest",
        "options": {
          "temperature": 0.4
        }
      },
      "id": "98504c3e-c98e-4399-b937-ac1515993b06",
      "name": "Gemini Flash-Lite",
      "type": "@n8n/n8n-nodes-langchain.lmChatGoogleGemini",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        300,
        260
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "sessionIdType": "customKey",
        "sessionKey": "weekly-strategy-brief",
        "contextWindowLength": 6
      },
      "id": "e8cac6cc-62d4-40b3-9581-1f465641ac98",
      "name": "Window Buffer Memory",
      "type": "@n8n/n8n-nodes-langchain.memoryBufferWindow",
      "typeVersion": 1.3,
      "position": [
        440,
        260
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "descriptionType": "manual",
        "toolDescription": "Reads every logged competitor-intelligence item from the Intel_Log data table. Columns: date (logged), competitor, source_type, title, link, published, category (pricing/product_launch/hiring/partnership/campaign/other), impact_score (1-10), is_relevant, summary, reasoning, model_used, alerted.",
        "resource": "row",
        "operation": "get",
        "dataTableId": {
          "__rl": true,
          "value": "Intel_Log",
          "mode": "name"
        },
        "returnAll": true
      },
      "id": "5fd40959-55a6-4810-94b0-0d0e94e6328f",
      "name": "read_intel_log",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.dataTableTool",
      "typeVersion": 1.1,
      "position": [
        580,
        260
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "toolDescription": "Searches recent news (Google News RSS). Input: a short search query such as 'Asana pricing'. Returns RSS XML with titles, links and dates.",
        "url": "=https://news.google.com/rss/search?q={{ encodeURIComponent($fromAI('query', 'short news search query', 'string')) }}&hl=en-IN&gl=IN&ceid=IN:en",
        "options": {}
      },
      "id": "d661c1ce-e5b9-46bc-bcfb-0a9cf5e8111b",
      "name": "web_search",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.httpRequestTool",
      "typeVersion": 4.2,
      "position": [
        720,
        260
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "description": "Compares the last 30 days of logged competitor activity with the previous 30 days. Returns item counts, high-impact counts, average impact score and category mix per competitor. Input: a competitor name, or 'all'.",
        "workflowId": {
          "__rl": true,
          "value": "__COMPARE_WORKFLOW_ID__",
          "mode": "id"
        },
        "workflowInputs": {
          "mappingMode": "defineBelow",
          "value": {
            "competitor": "={{ $fromAI('competitor', 'Competitor name exactly as logged, or all', 'string') }}"
          },
          "matchingColumns": [],
          "schema": [
            {
              "id": "competitor",
              "displayName": "competitor",
              "required": false,
              "defaultMatch": false,
              "display": true,
              "canBeUsedToMatch": true,
              "type": "string",
              "removed": false
            }
          ],
          "attemptToConvertTypes": false,
          "convertFieldsToString": false
        }
      },
      "id": "49c0a36f-2b02-462d-9285-8d4856e4e0df",
      "name": "compare_with_last_month",
      "type": "@n8n/n8n-nodes-langchain.toolWorkflow",
      "typeVersion": 2.2,
      "position": [
        860,
        260
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "assignments": {
          "assignments": [
            {
              "id": "8e79575b-907d-43c4-b87f-7bbc4def216e",
              "name": "week",
              "value": "={{ $now.toFormat(\"kkkk-'W'WW\") }}",
              "type": "string"
            },
            {
              "id": "225b02aa-715d-4080-b43b-3afacdefde3b",
              "name": "brief_markdown",
              "value": "={{ $json.output }}",
              "type": "string"
            },
            {
              "id": "28e262eb-4ec5-4410-84cf-6b5ee238791d",
